            <ArticleTitle>Myocardial bridging as a cause of acute anterior myocardial infarction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>111-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myocardial bridging is systolic compression of an epicardial coronary arterial segment by overlying myocardium. It is a rare coronary anomaly, which is generally considered to be benign. It has been suggested that myocardial ischaemia may be seen. In this article, a case of myocardial infarction caused by myocardial bridging is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
